  "accepted": [
    "Actual bundled models read the retained selected-window phrase with client/desktop boxes; a blank target returns empty text/lines.",
    "Admitted OCR completion feeds private TextContains, gates done Pulse and delivers the existing KeyPulse to the exact owned receiver; original passthrough wheel remains observable.",
    "Capture grant denial precedes original/native delivery; the peer actor sees no other actor readings. Ordinary state and structured JSON Script state omit live text/boxes; opted-in GUI PNGs may show visible text.",
    "GUI literal Update/Apply/Arm remain explicit; Screen Tools Read text uses a fresh authorized snapshot. Normal Stop, client EOF and owned WM_CLOSE cleanup completed.",
    "Fixed neutral 0.5 mask classification, trusted shape/finite-mask checks and exact unclipped recognition-width guards retain unfiltered recognized text and existing observation authority/cleanup.",
    "Qualified source retains the six-file offline model closure and separate complete MIT component-adapter notice; this does not qualify a complete portable release."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only the recorded two owned normal-pump x64 targets, Latin phrase/blank samples and GUI controls are natively qualified; no broad OCR, dark-theme or arbitrary-application accuracy claim.",
    "Timeout, queue saturation, late completion, target/grant changes and saved-release faults rely on deterministic Rust coverage, not a new native fault matrix.",
    "No hardware/global input, RustDesk, external vision/LLM service, desktop-wide or same-process isolation, GUI-stall P1 fix, full Ultra parity or complete portable release is established."
  ],
